JavaScript:
Window_Base.prototype.drawIcon = function(iconIndex, x, y) {
    var bitmap = ImageManager.loadSystem('IconSet');
    var pw = Window_Base._iconWidth;
    var ph = Window_Base._iconHeight;
    var sx = iconIndex % 16 * pw;
    var sy = Math.floor(iconIndex / 16) * ph;
    this.contents.blt(bitmap, sx, sy, pw, ph, x, y);
};
But this was already made! So it was easy for me to use, I only had to know iconIndex (which I set with a plugin parameter) x, and y. For this status window bust I'd have to write a new function similar to this one, right? But the problem is, I don't really understand fully what's going on inside this one x')
I understand that it creates a bitmap object? and for that it uses
ImageManager.loadSystem('name of file')
. I noticed there are several like this, loadSystem, loadPicture, loadFace... all in rpg_managers.js. They ask for a filename, and a hue. That part is alright. I understand they all have to do with each folder.
(I wonder what I'd have to use if I wanted to let the parameter load a file instead of writing the path here? but that would be for later...)
Then there's all the pw, ph, sx and sy that I don't understand much. They are all used for the next function,
this.contents.blt()
, (why contents?). So I go search that... and I find this in rpg_core.js
JavaScript:
@method blt
 * @param {Bitmap} source The bitmap to draw
 * @param {Number} sx The x coordinate in the source
 * @param {Number} sy The y coordinate in the source
 * @param {Number} sw The width of the source image
 * @param {Number} sh The height of the source image
 * @param {Number} dx The x coordinate in the destination
 * @param {Number} dy The y coordinate in the destination
 * @param {Number} [dw=sw] The width to draw the image in the destination
 * @param {Number} [dh=sh] The height to draw the image in the destination
 */
Bitmap.prototype.blt = function(source, sx, sy, sw, sh, dx, dy, dw, dh) {
    dw = dw || sw;
    dh = dh || sh;
    if (sx >= 0 && sy >= 0 && sw > 0 && sh > 0 && dw > 0 && dh > 0 &&
            sx + sw <= source.width && sy + sh <= source.height) {
        this._context.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        this._context.drawImage(source._canvas, sx, sy, sw, sh, dx, dy, dw, dh);
        this._setDirty();
    }
};
Well, that explains some, sx and sy. But what is pw and ph? Width and height of... what? Aren't many parameters missing from drawIcon? (but it works fine). Then my head is kinda exploding from that if alone, I don't get what this._context.globalCompositeOperation is doing, nor this._context.drawImage, nor this._setDirty().
So that's where I'm at. What am I supposed to do here? Include a new drawThing() somewhere? What should I even write to make it work? I tried to write this code for Window_Status, which obviously doesn't work (it doesn't do anything) but honestly I made it last week and I don't fully understand what I was doing myself lmao
